{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TowerSpanReduction"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.unit_quad_scalar_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.unit_quad_scalar_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeSandwichReduces.lean#L344-L353","doc":"In that instance the quadratic scalar is `u - u⁻¹`, and it is non-zero as\nsoon as `u² ≠ 1` — so the three relations are consistent with `h ≠ 0`, which is\nthe Hecke case `h = q - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.braidedTower_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.braidedTower_unit","kind":"instance","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeSandwichReduces.lean#L336-L342","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.braid_forces_eq_of_commuting_involutions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.braid_forces_eq_of_commuting_involutions","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeSandwichReduces.lean#L312-L325","doc":"If two adjacent generators commute and both square to `1`, the braid relation\nforces them equal. So a commuting-involution tower is braided only if it is\nconstant — which is exactly why `InvolutionTowerWitness` is not an instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.disjointBlock_of_braided","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.disjointBlock_of_braided","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeSandwichReduces.lean#L299-L303","doc":"**The disjoint-block trace law on any braided tower**, unconditionally in the\ntower structure: only the three defining relations are assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.towerSpan_of_braided","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.towerSpan_of_braided","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeSandwichReduces.lean#L294-L297","doc":"**`TowerSpan` holds on any braided tower** — the hypothesis of\n`DisjointBlockTraceLaw` is discharged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.sandwichReduces_all","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.sandwichReduces_all","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeSandwichReduces.lean#L263-L292","doc":"**`SandwichReduces` holds at every level of a braided tower.**\n\nInduction on `M`. Below the bottom of the shift window the stage is `⊥`; at the\nbottom of the full window it is affine in `g 0`; above, the previous level's\ndecomposition (`step_of_sandwichReduces` applied to the induction hypothesis)\nsplits the element into a base part and sandwiches, and `base_conj` /\n`sandwich_conj` handle them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.sandwichReduces_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.sandwichReduces_zero","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeSandwichReduces.lean#L240-L259","doc":"The base case: at the bottom of the full shift window the stage is affine in\n`g 0`, so one quadratic and one braid application suffice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.shiftedUpTo_zero_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.shiftedUpTo_zero_le","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeSandwichReduces.lean#L225-L238","doc":"The bottom stage of the full shift window sits inside the subalgebra\ngenerated by `g 0`, because the quadratic relation makes `ginv 0` affine in\n`g 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.sandwichReduces_of_le_bot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.sandwichReduces_of_le_bot","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeSandwichReduces.lean#L210-L223","doc":"Below the bottom of the shift window the stage is trivial, and the quadratic\nrelation alone reduces the sandwich. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.sandwich_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.sandwich_conj","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeSandwichReduces.lean#L176-L206","doc":"The sandwich part is turned over by the braid relation:\n`g₂ (v g₁ w) g₂ = v (g₁ g₂ g₁) w = (v g₁) g₂ (g₁ w)`, and both outer factors have\nrisen one level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.base_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.base_conj","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeSandwichReduces.lean#L162-L174","doc":"The base part of a decomposed element collapses by the quadratic relation\nalone: `g₂ u g₂ = u g₂² = h • (u g₂) + u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.shiftedUpTo_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.shiftedUpTo_commute","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeSandwichReduces.lean#L146-L158","doc":"Everything in a stage capped at level `M` commutes with a generator at any\nlevel `> M + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.ginv_far","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.ginv_far","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeSandwichReduces.lean#L138-L144","doc":"The inverse generator inherits distant commutation, because the quadratic\nrelation makes it affine in `g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.BraidedTower.braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.BraidedTower.braid","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeSandwichReduces.lean#L134-L134","doc":"The braid relation on adjacent generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.BraidedTower.far","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.BraidedTower.far","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeSandwichReduces.lean#L132-L132","doc":"Distant generators commute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.BraidedTower.quad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.BraidedTower.quad","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeSandwichReduces.lean#L130-L130","doc":"The quadratic relation. In `H_n(q)` the scalar is `h = q - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.BraidedTower.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.BraidedTower.mk","kind":"ctor","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeSandwichReduces.lean#L128-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.BraidedTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces.BraidedTower","kind":"class","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeSandwichReduces.lean#L125-L134","doc":"**The braid-tower relations.** Three equations on the generator family of a\n`MarkovTrace`, each of them a defining relation of the Iwahori-Hecke algebra.\nNone of them mentions the trace. ","signatureChunk":0}]}